{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Returns a binwalk-style map of content embedded in one local file: findings[] each with type (PE, ELF, thin/fat Mach-O, ZIP plus its central-directory and end-of-central-directory records, gzip, zlib, xz, zstd, bzip2, 7z, CAB, PNG, JPEG, PDF, SQLite, DEX, Java class, DER/PEM/PKCS12, SquashFS, cpio, tar, uImage, DTB), file_offset, a derived size or null, confidence (high/medium/low), a validated flag and a description; plus padding_runs[] of 0x00/0xff and a bounded entropy_profile[]. Regions are located by a BinSight-authored magic table and confirmed by bounded header/structure checks; sizes are derived only where a format declares one. It is identification only: it never extracts, decompresses a full stream, writes a file, spawns a process, uses the network or runs the target, and reads the bytes once (256 MiB input cap, single pass, capped candidate and finding counts, 8 MiB output cap). Unknowns are explicit: null size means no declared length, validated=false means a magic-only match, unrecognized regions carry no finding, findings/padding/entropy report truncation via coverage, and limitations state that identification is not proof of content and absence of a finding is not proof of absence.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"path":"/artifacts/application"},{"entropy_window":4096,"max_findings":2000,"path":"/artifacts/firmware.bin"}],"properties":{"entropy_window":{"default":8192,"description":"Requested width in bytes of each entropy-profile sample; widened for very large files","maximum":1048576,"minimum":256,"type":"integer"},"max_findings":{"default":1000,"description":"Maximum number of identified regions to return, most confident and earliest first","maximum":10000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"Absolute filesystem path to the selected